# Keyboard never steals typing

Toolbar navigation (`h` `l` `j` `k`, and Home/End as toolbar jumps) is for **buttons and chips**. It is not for text fields.

## Do

- When focus is in `input`, `textarea`, or `contentEditable`, letter keys must type.
- Use `blockToolbarNavInTextField(e, active)` (or the same rule) before any toolbar move.
- Arrow keys may leave a field only at the caret edge (`AtMoveBoundary`).
- Prefer Tab to leave a field when in doubt.

## Do not

- Treat `h`/`l`/`j`/`k` like arrows while the caret is in a composer, search box, URL field, API key, or filter input.
- Jump to Clear / Send / next chip when the user types `l` or `h` in AI Chat.
- Assume “caret at end” means “ready to leave the field” for letter keys — that is the normal typing position.

## Examples

```text
❌ Pressing l in #chat-input focuses Clear
❌ Pressing h in an empty URL field leaves the field
✅ Typing hello in AI Chat stays in the input
✅ ArrowRight at end of input may move to Clear / Send
```
